[{:db/id "q-81098/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "dd1cc6dd-9d67-5b90-8ac8-bc058e1c33c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81098/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "3335272b-1466-5b2b-9c2e-eb80f3bc0c35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81098/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "ce41c1b2-83ff-599a-bbd5-92d83d9143de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81098/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "62c715db-cb24-51e8-9823-4c18f652cc6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81098/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "47ad0aab-fc84-5bb9-aaca-0945d6bf99b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81098/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4251c9c6-fdf9-5223-88ef-f8a83ccbe5e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81098/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-81098/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-81098/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-81098/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-81098/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-81098/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81098" :question/id #uuid "f6bed643-ce3e-507d-aa72-c9eaa603d013" :question/math-academy-id "q-81098" :question/problem "If the path $C$ is a part of the parabola $y={x}^{2}-x$ traversed from the point $A(0,0)$ to point $B(2,2),$ then ${\\int }_{C}2xy\\,dx+x\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our curve is given by the explicit Cartesian equation $y={x}^{2}-x.$ As a result, we obtain the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=t\\,i+({t}^{2}-t)\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,2]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=i+(2t-1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2xy\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2xy\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(2xy\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2t({t}^{2}-t)\\cdot 1+t(2t-1)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{t}^{3}-t\\,dt \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{{2}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}]-[0] \\\\  & =8-2 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81098/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f04a969-e7e0-592f-b5cd-e92fedb217a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81098"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-81178"] :question/problem "If the path $C$ is a part of the parabola $y=(x+1)^{2}$ traversed from the point $P(0,1)$ to point $Q(1,4),$ then ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{dx+dy}{y}=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our curve is given by the explicit Cartesian equation $y=(x+1)^{2}.$ As a result, we obtain the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=t\\,i+(t+1)^{2}\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,1]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=i+2(t+1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{dx+dy}{y} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{y}(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{y}(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1+2(t+1)}{(t+1)^{2}}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(t+1)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{t+1}\\,dt \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{t+1}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{1+1}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+1)]-[-\\frac{1}{0+1}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0+1)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]-[-1+0] \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-90848/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer/id #uuid "4188b0c3-b5bb-55df-b23b-6eda1f545865" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90848/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "bb812ea7-a296-5786-a89b-3bba9cc888b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90848/selection/cef844f984b60552a9c52522bddacb7f61630a8705246b75d7a6580f476f785f" :answer/id #uuid "29722e4b-6cf6-5cf9-8b52-7451d0ade62d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{40}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90848/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8" :answer/id #uuid "75779101-db5b-5d49-84a3-e4bf841bef31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90848/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "9f8e7330-8fb7-53e3-a350-b9c4ee4205b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90848/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "19f207d4-f525-51a0-9baf-5fba3eda5400" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90848/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8" :answer-field/choices ["q-90848/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" "q-90848/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" "q-90848/selection/cef844f984b60552a9c52522bddacb7f61630a8705246b75d7a6580f476f785f" "q-90848/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8" "q-90848/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90848" :question/id #uuid "c3320ba2-2de7-59d7-ba39-d983351db61e" :question/math-academy-id "q-90848" :question/problem "If the path $C$ is a part of the parabola $y={x}^{2}-1$ traversed from the point $A(0,-1)$ to point $B(2,3),$ then ${\\int }_{C}5{x}^{2}y\\,dx+{x}^{2}(y+1)\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our curve is given by the explicit Cartesian equation $y={x}^{2}-1.$ As a result, we obtain the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=t\\,i+({t}^{2}-1)\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,2]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=i+2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}5{x}^{2}y\\,dx+{x}^{2}(y+1)\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}5{x}^{2}y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+{x}^{2}(y+1)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(5{x}^{2}y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+{x}^{2}(y+1)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}5{t}^{2}({t}^{2}-1)\\cdot 1+{t}^{2}({t}^{2}-1+1)\\cdot 2t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}5{t}^{4}-5{t}^{2}+2{t}^{5}\\,dt \\\\  & ={[{t}^{5}-\\frac{5}{3}{t}^{3}+\\frac{{t}^{6}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[{2}^{5}-\\frac{5}{3}(2)^{3}+\\frac{{2}^{6}}{3}]-[0] \\\\  & =32-\\frac{40}{3}+\\frac{64}{3} \\\\  & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-90848/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f04a969-e7e0-592f-b5cd-e92fedb217a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90848"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124656/selection/21c43f94ffeb019f2dd7c1090a71b5045b163c989652b5d5124fd2bf71898106" :answer/id #uuid "f2151f28-66ff-5cda-9211-5906f7882366" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t(1-4{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124656/selection/614a67c78ad16be048d9c74bb294d6ef57362e6d37a03b2c9a70104f6e46830c" :answer/id #uuid "6de58419-69b4-5be3-bcbc-a466ce4ffc80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t(1-4{cos}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124656/selection/5d49727387e2e7a872a42ef10787560a566d946d869ad10bc32d3b829d07f1b9" :answer/id #uuid "99f7b5e3-b4e0-5cd4-b4cd-b628df411ef1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t(1-2{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124656/selection/8a586a003da5b3c2814085d576e70f0f5f73841b6167b6ea00affe9f070db2bd" :answer/id #uuid "d619cdef-c048-54c6-b481-b788d0467834" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t(1-2{cos}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124656/selection/8412b5f32b6482f3dd98bd16ea37713192f9ce1996f62d97aec5e7e3c7dbd07f" :answer/id #uuid "194cbdfc-f0e6-5b10-941a-073ef36a1618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124656/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4506bc4-5dbe-5b03-8639-77e63c997b93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124656/selection/21c43f94ffeb019f2dd7c1090a71b5045b163c989652b5d5124fd2bf71898106" :answer-field/choices ["q-124656/selection/21c43f94ffeb019f2dd7c1090a71b5045b163c989652b5d5124fd2bf71898106" "q-124656/selection/614a67c78ad16be048d9c74bb294d6ef57362e6d37a03b2c9a70104f6e46830c" "q-124656/selection/5d49727387e2e7a872a42ef10787560a566d946d869ad10bc32d3b829d07f1b9" "q-124656/selection/8a586a003da5b3c2814085d576e70f0f5f73841b6167b6ea00affe9f070db2bd" "q-124656/selection/8412b5f32b6482f3dd98bd16ea37713192f9ce1996f62d97aec5e7e3c7dbd07f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124656" :question/id #uuid "1cc72486-d161-51c9-81d8-95cb93b64485" :question/math-academy-id "q-124656" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}y\\,dx+x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is part of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $A(2,0)$ to the point $B(-2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $C$ is a circle of radius $2$ centered at the origin, it can be parametrized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,\\pi ]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}y\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{x}^{2}y\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+x\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}y\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}+x\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}\\cdot (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-16{sin}^{2}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t(1-4{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124656/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5b5c517-8e13-5b70-bd1f-15ae495f0632"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124656"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124661/selection/a996cecead059c2e05b8ded2ceb60e4e2170a4344e0c20625524ed13b23c6fbe" :answer/id #uuid "5834f9df-e912-5850-8c34-b424f767e97e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124661/selection/a7218079be5401cd39608c49417e0d290c58cb6901a7da64771bd072f8d49678" :answer/id #uuid "7ce5dc3a-e973-568d-84b3-65b310c6a3de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi +1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124661/selection/358ed8369e6ebfc562322cdaba733c6146f92bfb7631aaaaa2bc4113e2924ebb" :answer/id #uuid "9ac7a92e-45db-5339-954a-3d12f0af502b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12\\pi -5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124661/selection/e858e73de7e1773ea4462bd9ff370f3911e507e8aae90f258c3076dd5f89ef68" :answer/id #uuid "5fc63b1a-0f79-5065-ab5a-4326d53873c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6\\pi -5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124661/selection/cd8957b3e03d9fbea87893281373eded912abde9aae6462917a9ce8659b8cc99" :answer/id #uuid "63102b81-f990-580b-9d83-074239c7f80d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124661/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "63838486-62db-561a-b0a0-898d48bc4de6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124661/selection/e858e73de7e1773ea4462bd9ff370f3911e507e8aae90f258c3076dd5f89ef68" :answer-field/choices ["q-124661/selection/a996cecead059c2e05b8ded2ceb60e4e2170a4344e0c20625524ed13b23c6fbe" "q-124661/selection/a7218079be5401cd39608c49417e0d290c58cb6901a7da64771bd072f8d49678" "q-124661/selection/358ed8369e6ebfc562322cdaba733c6146f92bfb7631aaaaa2bc4113e2924ebb" "q-124661/selection/e858e73de7e1773ea4462bd9ff370f3911e507e8aae90f258c3076dd5f89ef68" "q-124661/selection/cd8957b3e03d9fbea87893281373eded912abde9aae6462917a9ce8659b8cc99"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124661" :question/id #uuid "0814c9bc-122f-53c2-a756-b81f1b80f4de" :question/math-academy-id "q-124661" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}(x-y)\\,dx+(x+y)\\,dy,$ where $C$ is part of the ellipse $9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $(0,3)$ to the point $(-2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $2$ and $3,$ respectively, it can be parametrized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & ={x}^{′}(t)\\,i+{y}^{′}(t)\\,j=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x-y)\\,dx+(x+y)\\,dy & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(x-y)\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+(x+y)\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }((x-y)\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}+(x+y)\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+6{sin}^{2}⁡t+6{cos}^{2}⁡t+9\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+6\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+6\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+6t]}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[(-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )+6\\pi )-(-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+3\\pi )] \\\\  & =(-\\frac{5}{4}+6\\pi )-(\\frac{5}{4}+3\\pi ) \\\\  & =3\\pi -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pi -5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124661/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5b5c517-8e13-5b70-bd1f-15ae495f0632"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124661"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
